   "body": [
    {
     "t": "h3",
     "a": {
      "id": "the-problem-the-250-item-limit"
     },
     "c": [
      {
       "t": "strong",
       "c": [
        "The Problem: The 250 Item Limit"
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "ul",
     "c": [
      "\n",
      {
       "t": "li",
       "c": [
        {
         "t": "strong",
         "c": [
          "The Requirement:"
         ]
        },
        " Organizations often need custom reports, such as a comprehensive list of all disabled accounts that still retain active access entitlements across all sources."
       ]
      },
      "\n",
      {
       "t": "li",
       "c": [
        {
         "t": "strong",
         "c": [
          "The Governance Gap:"
         ]
        },
        " While there are out-of-the-box ways to pull this data using external PowerShell scripts or PTA, keeping the entire process native inside Identity Security Cloud (ISC) Workflows is ideal for simplicity and maintenance."
       ]
      },
      "\n",
      {
       "t": "li",
       "c": [
        {
         "t": "strong",
         "c": [
          "The Risk:"
         ]
        },
        " Workflows have a strict execution time limit and no native pagination support for HTTP requests. If an API returns more than 250 items, a standard workflow simply cannot process the rest of the data."
       ]
      },
      "\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "h3",
     "a": {
      "id": "the-architecture-custom-reports-with-workflow-pagination"
     },
     "c": [
      {
       "t": "strong",
       "c": [
        "The Architecture: Custom Reports with Workflow Pagination"
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "ul",
     "c": [
      "\n",
      {
       "t": "li",
       "c": [
        {
         "t": "strong",
         "c": [
          "The “Why”:"
         ]
        },
        " By using serial loops and advanced variable updating, we can build robust, paginated reports and send them natively via email without needing any external infrastructure."
       ]
      },
      "\n",
      {
       "t": "li",
       "c": [
        {
         "t": "strong",
         "c": [
          "The Workflows:"
         ]
        },
        " We split this into two components.\n",
        {
         "t": "ol",
         "c": [
          "\n",
          {
           "t": "li",
           "c": [
            {
             "t": "strong",
             "c": [
              "Launcher Workflow:"
             ]
            },
            " Starts with an Interactive Trigger and a form. This allows an admin to select individual sources or “All Sources” to run the report against. It then defines the necessary variables and triggers the worker workflow."
           ]
          },
          "\n"
         ]
        },
        "\n"
       ]
      },
      "\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "div",
     "a": {
      "class": "d-wrap",
      "data-wrap": "center"
     },
     "c": [
      "\n",
      {
       "t": "lightbox",
       "a": {
        "full": "https://global.discourse-cdn.com/sailpoint/original/3X/4/6/462640715f8f405cc696bc6cf9e983ab7c8f58c3.png",
        "src": "https://global.discourse-cdn.com/sailpoint/optimized/3X/4/6/462640715f8f405cc696bc6cf9e983ab7c8f58c3_2_456x500.png",
        "srcSet": "https://global.discourse-cdn.com/sailpoint/optimized/3X/4/6/462640715f8f405cc696bc6cf9e983ab7c8f58c3_2_456x500.png, https://global.discourse-cdn.com/sailpoint/optimized/3X/4/6/462640715f8f405cc696bc6cf9e983ab7c8f58c3_2_684x750.png 1.5x, https://global.discourse-cdn.com/sailpoint/original/3X/4/6/462640715f8f405cc696bc6cf9e983ab7c8f58c3.png 2x",
        "alt": "InteractiveDisabledAccountsWithAccessReport20260625",
        "width": "456",
